<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Road</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal Road was an ancient highway of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> running about 2,700 kilometres from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardis">Sardis</a>, with relay stations along its length. Royal couriers using fresh horses could carry messages across it in around seven days. The Achaemenid Empire profile presents it as a key instrument of imperial communication and trade, building on earlier Assyrian road systems.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/royal-road.jpg" alt="Royal Road" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original creator: Mossmaps Corrections according to Oxford Atlas of World History 2002, The Times Atlas of World Hist... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Achaemenid_Empire_at_its_greatest_extent_according_to_Oxford_Atlas_of_World_History_2002.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
